name:    zellij
what:    starting and attaching sessions from the shell
check:   zellij
install: curl -4L https://github.com/zellij-org/zellij/releases/latest/download/zellij-x86_64-unknown-linux-musl.tar.gz \| tar xz -C ~/.local/bin
docs:    zellij --help
probe:   help

# WSL2 note: the plain download times out on GitHub release assets. `curl -4`
# fetches the same URL in about a second — a HEAD request succeeding proves
# nothing, because it is the large transfer that stalls.

= STARTING
zellij           | start. The bottom bar lists every key, always
zellij -s work   | start a named session
@zellij attach   | attach to an existing one; `zellij a` is the short form
zellij ls        | list them
zellij ka        | kill every session
zellij da        | delete every dead session's state

= CHECKING IT OVER
zellij setup --check | what it found: config path, shell, terminal features
zellij setup --dump-config | the full default config, to copy bits out of
zellij --version | the version, which decides which config keys parse

= ALL FLAGS (from --help)
